  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-7041" textLabel="CPLX-7041" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-7041" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="775" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana MVK&lt;/i&gt; gene was heterologously expressed in two &lt;i&gt;Saccharomyces cerevisiae&lt;/i&gt; mutant strains, the temperature-sensitive mutant &lt;i&gt;MN19-34&lt;/i&gt; (&lt;i&gt;MAT&amp;alpha;, erg19-34, ura3-1, trp1-1&lt;/i&gt;) and a strain containing a disrupted &lt;i&gt;erg19&lt;/i&gt; copy. The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; gene restored growth for both strains albeit not to wildtype levels |CITS:[10344201]|. The protein is therefore thought to act as mevalonate diphosphate decarboxylase in the mevalonate pathway. Yeast two-hybrid studied showed that the protein forms a homodimeric complex. Incidentally, it was also shown to be able to interact with its &lt;i&gt;Saccharomyces&lt;/i&gt; homolog to form a heterodimer |CITS:[10344201]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-7041" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT2G38700-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-12485" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="2" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_10344201" />
    </Group>
  </Groups>
